# Gap Analysis – Patient Appointment Management

| Current State                                                | Gap                         | Proposed State                                   |
| ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| Patients receive basic appointment details                   | No proactive reminder       | Automated appointment reminders                  |
| Patients cannot easily confirm attendance                    | No confirmation mechanism   | Appointment confirmation                         |
| Rescheduling may require staff assistance                    | Manual rescheduling process | Self-service rescheduling                        |
| Cancellation reasons are not consistently captured           | Limited cancellation data   | Standardized cancellation reasons                |
| Staff manually follow up with patients                       | High manual effort          | System identifies unconfirmed appointments       |
| Limited visibility into no-shows                             | No centralized reporting    | Appointment performance dashboard                |
| No-show information is mainly reviewed after the appointment | Limited proactive action    | Early identification of unconfirmed appointments |

## Key Gaps Identified

1. Lack of automated reminders
2. Lack of appointment confirmation
3. Manual rescheduling process
4. Inconsistent cancellation tracking
5. Manual staff follow-up
6. Limited reporting and analytics

## Business Impact

These gaps can contribute to missed appointments, unused appointment slots, increased administrative workload, and reduced visibility into appointment performance.

## Recommended Improvement

Implement an appointment management solution with automated reminders, confirmation, rescheduling, cancellation tracking, and management reporting.
